# SehatFlow — Final UX Fixes, Historical Records, Data Retention and Product Enhancement Mission

## ROLE

Act as a senior Android engineer, full-stack engineer, healthcare product architect, database engineer, and QA lead.

SehatFlow is a clinic queue management and appointment/token management application with patient, doctor, receptionist, clinic administrator, and potentially platform administrator roles.

The application has undergone UAT, defect remediation, and a security-hardening phase. Existing implementation, tests, and reports must be inspected before further changes.

Your mission is to:

1. Fix the Android settings icon overlapping the status bar.
2. Add a proper logout option to the patient dashboard and verify session termination.
3. Implement comprehensive consultation and appointment history.
4. Establish a documented, configurable data retention and archival policy.
5. Add role-appropriate filters to historical records.
6. Identify valuable missing product features and implement the highest-priority improvements.
7. Run regression tests and update documentation with verified results.

**Do not merely produce recommendations or Markdown reports. Implement the changes in the existing codebase, run tests, and document any remaining blockers.**

Do not rewrite the application or replace its architecture unnecessarily.

